-- title:
--   Equivalence of weak and trace-norm compactness for density operators
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be an arbitrary complete complex Hilbert space, and let $\mathcal D(H)$ be the set of positive trace-class operators on $H$ with trace one. Let $K\subseteq\mathcal D(H)$ be any set. Give $\mathcal D(H)$ the weak topology generated by all functions $\rho\mapsto\operatorname{Tr}(\rho A)$, where $A$ ranges over all bounded operators on $H$. Then
--
--   $$
--   K\text{ is compact in this weak topology}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad K\text{ is compact in the trace-norm topology}.
--   $$
--
--   Here the trace norm is $\lVert T\rVert_1=\operatorname{Tr}\sqrt{T^*T}$. No separability, finite dimension, or nonemptiness of $K$ is required. This equivalence supplies the compactness criterion used in the paper's existence theorem for maximally resourceful states.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The Hilbert basis is arbitrary and need not be countable. The source calls the bounded-observable topology the weak operator topology; its explicit trace tests determine the topology in the formal statement.
-- source:
--   General Quantum Resource Theories: Distillation, Formation and Consistent Resource Measures, arXiv:2002.02458v3, PDF p. 25, Lemma 28

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intake100_P50

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P50

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Dependency50.P13

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]

/-- Lemma 28, arXiv:2002.02458v3, PDF p.25 (topologies defined on PDF p.4).
For every set of normal density operators, compactness for all bounded trace
pairings is equivalent to trace-norm compactness. No compactness of the entire
density-operator space, nonemptiness of the set, finite dimension, or
separability of the Hilbert space is assumed. -/
theorem lemma28_compactness_iff_traceNorm {I : Type*}
    (b : HilbertBasis I ℂ H) (K : Set (State b)) :
    (letI : TopologicalSpace (State b) := stateBoundedWeakTopology b
     IsCompact K) ↔ TraceCompactStates K := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P50

end
